  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since the reactant is a <math><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> alkyl halide, so in the presence of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo></math> it will follow E2 path rather than <math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mtext>S</mtext>   <mtext>N</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>2,</mtext></mrow></math> so path <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is not feasible.<br />The possible product by path <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/6652f935-2334-488a-a9bc-a24063a6f56b.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:5.775in;height:1.33333in\" />",
